WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.545 --> 00:00:03.878
(Overwatch theme music)

00:00:08.971 --> 00:00:10.205
- [Hammeh] And welcome.

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:11.221
I'm Hammeh, and in this series,

00:00:11.221 --> 00:00:12.539
we're discovering the lore, backstory,

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:14.955
and characters of Overwatch's
heroes, including more detail

00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:17.364
through their in-game voice
lines and interactions.

00:00:17.364 --> 00:00:18.475
Before any map starts

00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:20.025
and during the game on various triggers,

00:00:20.025 --> 00:00:22.086
Overwatch heroes chatter
with and react to each other

00:00:22.086 --> 00:00:23.473
in some funny ingame ways.

00:00:23.473 --> 00:00:25.093
These give us some great extra insights

00:00:25.093 --> 00:00:27.771
into hero character,
interests, and backstories too.

00:00:27.771 --> 00:00:29.977
In this video, we're
looking at Roadhog's story

00:00:29.977 --> 00:00:31.923
through his interactions with other heroes

00:00:31.923 --> 00:00:33.539
and the world around him.

00:00:33.539 --> 00:00:35.251
Currently an internationally
wanted criminal,

00:00:35.251 --> 00:00:37.676
the life of Mako Rutledge
wasn't always this way.

00:00:37.676 --> 00:00:39.148
Once a rebel with a cause,

00:00:39.148 --> 00:00:41.254
following the theft and
then destruction of his home

00:00:41.254 --> 00:00:43.191
and the lands around
it, he's now only known

00:00:43.191 --> 00:00:44.733
as the ruthless wanted killer

00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:47.165
and internationally
wanted criminal Roadhog.

00:00:47.165 --> 00:00:48.549
Firstly, we'll discover
Roadhog's background

00:00:48.549 --> 00:00:49.650
and origin story.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.453
In an Overwatch future,
Omnica Corporations Omnium's

00:00:52.453 --> 00:00:55.410
promised to revolutionise
robotic manufacturing.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.179
The automated construction machinery,

00:00:57.179 --> 00:00:59.161
backed by self improving
software algorithms,

00:00:59.161 --> 00:01:01.367
were set to usher in a new economic age

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.197
on par with the industrial revolution

00:01:03.197 --> 00:01:05.015
or the invention of the production line

00:01:05.015 --> 00:01:06.049
in the history books.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:08.313
Installed on every continent
and powered by fusion cores,

00:01:08.313 --> 00:01:10.737
Australia's omnium was
located in the outback,

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:13.460
which was only populated with
a scattering of solar farmers,

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.730
survivalists, and those
seeking solitude at the time.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.468
When the First Omnic Crisis struck

00:01:18.468 --> 00:01:20.549
and waves of omnics emerged from omniums

00:01:20.549 --> 00:01:22.094
that were thought to be defunct,

00:01:22.094 --> 00:01:23.591
the residence of the Australian outback

00:01:23.591 --> 00:01:25.505
would've been first in the line of fire.

00:01:25.505 --> 00:01:27.859
Australia as a country
was hit particularly hard,

00:01:27.859 --> 00:01:30.896
almost being destroyed as
a result in the conflict.

00:01:30.896 --> 00:01:32.467
After the crisis was brought to an end

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:33.774
by the actions of Overwatch,

00:01:33.774 --> 00:01:36.587
it appears that unlike the
uncommunicative omnic forces

00:01:36.587 --> 00:01:38.696
that had started the
war, by its conclusion,

00:01:38.696 --> 00:01:40.649
there were independent, self aware omnics,

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:43.398
even with omnic central
command protocols destroyed

00:01:43.398 --> 00:01:46.161
and with the God AIs that
played some part in the crisis

00:01:46.161 --> 00:01:47.619
put into containment.

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:48.934
The Australian government,

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:50.573
rebuilding like so many other countries,

00:01:50.573 --> 00:01:52.850
must have had a large enough
amount of these omnics

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.254
remaining in Australia to
consider drastic action

00:01:55.254 --> 00:01:57.390
and to be forced to negotiate.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.375
In an attempt to
establish a longterm peace

00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:01.649
with these remaining
omnics, government officials

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:04.171
gifted them the Australian
omnium and the surrounding area

00:02:04.171 --> 00:02:06.256
in a reservation style agreement.

00:02:06.256 --> 00:02:07.696
And in this attempted peace deal,

00:02:07.696 --> 00:02:10.628
nearby residents ended up
losing their homes as a result,

00:02:10.628 --> 00:02:12.355
including a young Mako Rutledge,

00:02:12.355 --> 00:02:14.190
possibly in his early
twenties at the time.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:15.887
We know nothing of Mako's early years,

00:02:15.887 --> 00:02:17.744
but perhaps there's
some clues in his skins,

00:02:17.744 --> 00:02:19.811
with the toa, tribal looking skin.

00:02:19.811 --> 00:02:22.038
Toa are small artefacts made by members

00:02:22.038 --> 00:02:24.022
of one south Australian aboriginal tribe,

00:02:24.022 --> 00:02:25.519
so perhaps that's a hint

00:02:25.519 --> 00:02:27.591
as to some of Mako's
ancestry in some form.

00:02:27.591 --> 00:02:29.660
Whatever his past, young
Rutledge was furious

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.349
at the sacrifice of his home,

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:33.107
and joined other similar minded people

00:02:33.107 --> 00:02:34.962
and forming the Australian
Liberation Front,

00:02:34.962 --> 00:02:37.179
an organisation dedicated
to taking back the land

00:02:37.179 --> 00:02:39.190
that their government
had given to the omnics.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:41.709
Fighting escalated until
the rebels sabotaged

00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:43.333
the omnium's fusion core,

00:02:43.333 --> 00:02:45.941
resulting in a fusion explosion
that destroyed the facility,

00:02:45.941 --> 00:02:48.329
irradiated the surrounding
region with fallout,

00:02:48.329 --> 00:02:50.542
and littering the outback
with debris and metal

00:02:50.542 --> 00:02:52.521
for kilometres around, forever altering

00:02:52.521 --> 00:02:53.960
the landscape of the area.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.027
Amidst this wreckage,
there were some survivors.

00:02:56.027 --> 00:02:57.595
Some people banded together

00:02:57.595 --> 00:02:58.953
and called themselves the junkers,

00:02:58.953 --> 00:03:00.687
scavenging the husk of the omnium,

00:03:00.687 --> 00:03:02.711
recovering metal,
components, and other salvage

00:03:02.711 --> 00:03:05.743
and formed a lawless, cutthroat
society in its shadow.

00:03:05.743 --> 00:03:08.162
The main settlement in the
area became known as Junkertown

00:03:08.162 --> 00:03:09.477
and this would be a key location

00:03:09.477 --> 00:03:11.089
in not only the stories
of not only Roadhog,

00:03:11.089 --> 00:03:12.312
but also Junkrat.

00:03:12.312 --> 00:03:14.723
Mako watched as his home
became an apocalyptic wasteland

00:03:14.723 --> 00:03:16.776
and he changed forever,
in attempting to adapt

00:03:16.776 --> 00:03:19.411
to this new, broken world
he once called home.

00:03:19.411 --> 00:03:21.581
Becoming a junker
enforcer, he donned a mask,

00:03:21.581 --> 00:03:23.196
took to the highways of the outback

00:03:23.196 --> 00:03:24.802
in the area surrounding the omnium,

00:03:24.802 --> 00:03:26.751
and little by little,
the person that he was

00:03:26.751 --> 00:03:28.378
became a thing of the past.

00:03:28.378 --> 00:03:31.354
The last vestiges of Mako's
personality faded away

00:03:31.354 --> 00:03:32.848
and Roadhog was born.

00:03:32.848 --> 00:03:34.263
Known as a ruthless killer

00:03:34.263 --> 00:03:36.436
with a well earned reputation
for cruelty and destruction,

00:03:36.436 --> 00:03:38.359
Roadhog's currently
working as a bodyguard,

00:03:38.359 --> 00:03:41.033
keeping Junkrat safe in
exchange for a 50/50 share

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.169
of whatever valuable secret he discovered

00:03:43.169 --> 00:03:45.207
in the husk of the Australian omnium.

00:03:45.207 --> 00:03:47.111
Whether they're escaping
the gangs and bounty hunters

00:03:47.111 --> 00:03:49.265
after Junkrat or just
expanding their horizons,

00:03:49.265 --> 00:03:51.012
the pair have now left the outback

00:03:51.012 --> 00:03:53.485
and are currently embarked on
an international crime spree.

00:03:53.485 --> 00:03:55.449
We've seen them in the UK in King's Row,

00:03:55.449 --> 00:03:56.653
stealing the crown jewels,

00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:58.496
robbing the vault in
Dorado, Mexico for gold,

00:03:58.496 --> 00:04:00.584
and even breaking into
ice cream trucks in Paris

00:04:00.584 --> 00:04:03.740
and taking arcade toys in
what may be Hanamura, Japan.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.637
We also know that Roadhog
as been through Sydney

00:04:05.637 --> 00:04:06.911
before travelling worldwide,

00:04:06.911 --> 00:04:08.821
as detailed in their comic, Going Legit,

00:04:08.821 --> 00:04:10.574
when what they thought
was a legitimate job

00:04:10.574 --> 00:04:12.538
turned out to be a setup
for an insurance scam.

00:04:12.538 --> 00:04:15.090
The pair got an explosive
and murderous revenge

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:18.035
with the presumed death of
the CEO or senior member

00:04:18.035 --> 00:04:19.762
of a company called Hyde Global.

00:04:19.762 --> 00:04:22.892
The motto of apparently no job
too big, no score too small,

00:04:22.892 --> 00:04:25.026
and gracing crimestopper
programmes the world over,

00:04:25.026 --> 00:04:27.555
will a similarly reluctant
Mako get his share

00:04:27.555 --> 00:04:28.958
of Junkrat's treasure?

00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:30.348
Is the criminal life all there is now

00:04:30.348 --> 00:04:31.463
for the displaced Junker,

00:04:31.463 --> 00:04:33.304
as he's almost entering his fifties?

00:04:33.304 --> 00:04:35.225
There's one thing we
can definitely count on:

00:04:35.225 --> 00:04:38.774
as long as he's teamed up with
the anarchaic Jamison Fawkes,

00:04:38.774 --> 00:04:40.934
trouble is never going to be far away

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:42.859
for the hog of our hearts.

00:04:42.859 --> 00:04:44.317
Whatever kind of person he was

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.723
before the Ausralian omnium's destruction,

00:04:45.723 --> 00:04:47.631
Roadhog's certainly a
man of violent actions

00:04:47.631 --> 00:04:49.065
and few words now.

00:04:49.065 --> 00:04:51.708
In fact, a lot of his words
are to do with violence.

00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:54.875
- [Roadhog] Welcome to the apocalypse.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:58.633
Violence is usually the answer.

00:05:01.377 --> 00:05:03.460
I'm a one man apocalypse.

00:05:06.536 --> 00:05:09.703
Go on, ask me what the other one says.

00:05:11.106 --> 00:05:12.189
It says left.

00:05:14.279 --> 00:05:15.324
- [Hammeh] However, humour wise,

00:05:15.324 --> 00:05:16.954
Roadhog does see the
funny side of some things,

00:05:16.954 --> 00:05:19.044
even if it's mostly violence related.

00:05:19.044 --> 00:05:21.499
He's clearly a fan of pigs
from his various stickers,

00:05:21.499 --> 00:05:22.987
ornaments on his bike, and other things

00:05:22.987 --> 00:05:24.990
and there's quite a few
references to those too.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.983
- [Roadhog] Here, little piggy.

00:05:27.983 --> 00:05:29.983
Say bacon one more time.

00:05:32.691 --> 00:05:36.331
Oops. (chuckling)

00:05:36.331 --> 00:05:37.664
Want some candy?

00:05:39.388 --> 00:05:40.864
- [Hammeh] As well as the most threatening

00:05:40.864 --> 00:05:43.163
Halloween statement I've probably heard.

00:05:43.163 --> 00:05:44.791
And when Roadhog kills enemy Reaper,

00:05:44.791 --> 00:05:46.255
he'll occasionally throw
out a little sarcastic,

00:05:46.255 --> 00:05:48.746
in my head anyway, compliment

00:05:48.746 --> 00:05:50.505
- [Roadhog] Nice mask.

00:05:50.505 --> 00:05:52.314
- [Hammeh] From one
mask wearer to another.

00:05:52.314 --> 00:05:55.358
- [Roadhog] No pain, no gain.

00:05:55.358 --> 00:05:57.525
- [Hammeh] In terms of that
last line, I doubt he's talking

00:05:57.525 --> 00:05:59.533
in the fitness motivational sense there.

00:05:59.533 --> 00:06:01.128
Someone else's pain will probably result

00:06:01.128 --> 00:06:03.428
in some gain for Roadhog and Junkrat.

00:06:03.428 --> 00:06:05.438
Although he's known as
a criminal killer now,

00:06:05.438 --> 00:06:07.416
Roadhog does have a philosophical side

00:06:07.416 --> 00:06:08.896
that comes out from time to time.

00:06:08.896 --> 00:06:10.721
Here's some examples of his musings.

00:06:10.721 --> 00:06:12.526
- [Roadhog] Everyone has a plan,

00:06:12.526 --> 00:06:15.443
till they get punched in the mouth.

00:06:16.424 --> 00:06:20.591
Life is pain, so is death. (chuckling)

00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:28.817
Only thing you can count
on in this broken world.

00:06:31.003 --> 00:06:32.503
We're all animals.

00:06:35.069 --> 00:06:36.819
What's mine, is mine.

00:06:38.188 --> 00:06:40.016
- [Hammeh] And it does feel
like occasional flashes

00:06:40.016 --> 00:06:41.857
of a person beyond the violent killer

00:06:41.857 --> 00:06:43.383
that Roadhog is known as now.

00:06:43.383 --> 00:06:45.754
He occasionally expresses
very out of character

00:06:45.754 --> 00:06:47.586
or opposite sentiments to his desires

00:06:47.586 --> 00:06:49.036
for violence and destruction.

00:06:49.036 --> 00:06:50.619
- [Roadhog] Pretty.

00:06:51.989 --> 00:06:53.906
Thanks for noticing me.

00:06:54.976 --> 00:06:56.476
Aw, that's no fun.

00:06:58.231 --> 00:06:59.564
I need my space.

00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:02.325
- [Hammeh] In some of
the clips, we see Roadhog

00:07:02.325 --> 00:07:03.904
is stealing things like ice cream

00:07:03.904 --> 00:07:05.505
or robbing an ice cream truck,

00:07:05.505 --> 00:07:07.494
taking away handfuls
of toys from an arcade.

00:07:07.494 --> 00:07:09.680
He does have this
mildly, how can I put it,

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.716
childish flash of innocence, maybe,

00:07:11.716 --> 00:07:14.020
a more sombre, not Sombra, personality.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.653
Indeed, thanks for noticing me,

00:07:15.653 --> 00:07:17.660
that line is also a line that Eeyore says

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.404
in the Winnie the Pooh children's books,

00:07:19.404 --> 00:07:20.605
if you're familiar with those.

00:07:20.605 --> 00:07:22.012
Eeyore is a bit of a gloomy donkey,

00:07:22.012 --> 00:07:23.248
bit of a pessimist,

00:07:23.248 --> 00:07:25.793
and kind of just wants
to be included and liked.

00:07:25.793 --> 00:07:27.710
That does feel similar
to some of the vibes

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.707
that I think Roadhog gives on occasion.

00:07:29.707 --> 00:07:30.671
What do you reckon?

00:07:30.671 --> 00:07:31.745
Okay, time for the reference game.

00:07:31.745 --> 00:07:33.300
There's not a huge amount
with our Hog friend,

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.686
but I'll leave a gap as always

00:07:34.686 --> 00:07:35.742
so you can have a guess at this one.

00:07:35.742 --> 00:07:38.339
- [Roadhog] So much
trauma going on in L-B-C,

00:07:38.339 --> 00:07:41.839
it's kind of hard being Road H-O-single-G.

00:07:43.846 --> 00:07:45.265
- [Hammeh] That's from the
famous Snoop Dogg track,

00:07:45.265 --> 00:07:46.643
Gin and Juice of course.

00:07:46.643 --> 00:07:48.270
Can't believe that's 20+ years old now.

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:50.166
LBC, Long Beach City, California,

00:07:50.166 --> 00:07:52.070
hip hop home of Warren G amongst others.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:53.742
I'll leave it to folks
more educated than I am

00:07:53.742 --> 00:07:55.774
in hip hop history to
take over from there.

00:07:55.774 --> 00:07:57.306
But Roadhog, clearly a fan.

00:07:57.306 --> 00:07:58.727
That one's not actually
in the game anymore,

00:07:58.727 --> 00:08:00.621
I don't think, so maybe it was left out

00:08:00.621 --> 00:08:01.853
for copyright reasons.

00:08:01.853 --> 00:08:03.012
Reference wise, of course,

00:08:03.012 --> 00:08:04.625
Roadhog is a whole bunch of references

00:08:04.625 --> 00:08:06.832
in terms of Junkenstein's Revenge.

00:08:06.832 --> 00:08:08.876
The presence of Roadhog
as Junkenstein's Monster

00:08:08.876 --> 00:08:10.164
is pretty accurate.

00:08:10.164 --> 00:08:12.165
A lot of people think the
monster is called Frankenstein,

00:08:12.165 --> 00:08:13.436
but that's of course
the name of the doctor

00:08:13.436 --> 00:08:15.236
from the book by Mary Shelley.

00:08:15.236 --> 00:08:16.579
He's got a lot of amazing voice work

00:08:16.579 --> 00:08:17.625
I've gone through in other videos,

00:08:17.625 --> 00:08:19.264
so here's just a couple
of my favourite lines.

00:08:19.264 --> 00:08:21.097
- [Roadhog] I'm alive!

00:08:23.413 --> 00:08:27.330
They called me a monster,
so I'll be a monster.

00:08:29.092 --> 00:08:30.063
- [Hammeh] Finally, although I don't think

00:08:30.063 --> 00:08:31.689
it's quoted directly
by Roadhog or Junkrat,

00:08:31.689 --> 00:08:34.685
although Ana's witness me
is an obvious reference,

00:08:34.685 --> 00:08:37.650
Mad Max and the Australian
post-apocalyptic future

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:40.674
are clearly a big inspiration
for Roadhog and Junkrat.

00:08:40.674 --> 00:08:42.238
The Many Mothers from Mad Max, Fury Road

00:08:42.238 --> 00:08:44.403
were part of the visual
inspiration for Ana's look

00:08:44.403 --> 00:08:46.825
and Junkrat and Roadhog's
whole design vibe

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:48.317
as well as their home and story

00:08:48.317 --> 00:08:50.494
definitely is an homage to the films.

00:08:50.494 --> 00:08:52.029
Roadhog doesn't have huge connexions

00:08:52.029 --> 00:08:53.107
with the Overwatch cast.

00:08:53.107 --> 00:08:54.564
A man of few words, of course,

00:08:54.564 --> 00:08:56.559
he still has a few
interactions with Junkrat.

00:08:56.559 --> 00:08:58.989
The troublesome twosome re
literally thick as thieves,

00:08:58.989 --> 00:09:00.521
Roadhog's in it for the money as we know,

00:09:00.521 --> 00:09:02.038
guarding Junkrat for a share

00:09:02.038 --> 00:09:04.103
of the mysterious treasure
that he possesses.

00:09:04.103 --> 00:09:06.307
Roadhog does grumble a
lot at Jamison Fawkes,

00:09:06.307 --> 00:09:08.232
but however well they don't get on,

00:09:08.232 --> 00:09:09.353
the two do seem to have

00:09:09.353 --> 00:09:10.879
the occasional comedy moment together.

00:09:10.879 --> 00:09:14.189
Roadhog of course complains
a lot about Junkrat.

00:09:14.189 --> 00:09:16.856
- [Roadhog] Do you ever shut up?

00:09:18.232 --> 00:09:21.065
Someday, I'm just gonna leave you.

00:09:22.404 --> 00:09:23.749
- [Hammeh] And when Roadhog asks Junkrat

00:09:23.749 --> 00:09:26.649
to stay out of trouble,
Junkrat swears that he will.

00:09:26.649 --> 00:09:29.210
- [Roadhog] Try and stay
out of trouble for once.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:30.968
- [Junkrat] I'll be on me best behaviour.

00:09:30.968 --> 00:09:33.106
- [Hammeh] I don't think he's
been too successful on that.

00:09:33.106 --> 00:09:35.370
Apparently Roadhog comes
up with the odd joke even,

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:36.411
according to Junkrat.

00:09:36.411 --> 00:09:37.527
- [Junkrat] You won't believe the joke

00:09:37.527 --> 00:09:42.294
old Pigface over there told
me the other day, right, Hog?

00:09:42.294 --> 00:09:45.076
- [Roadhog] Do you ever shut up?

00:09:45.076 --> 00:09:46.735
- [Hammeh] When Junkrat comments
on their combat techniques,

00:09:46.735 --> 00:09:48.394
Roadhog doesn't want any of it.

00:09:48.394 --> 00:09:51.541
- [Junkrat] You hook 'em, I'll cook 'em.

00:09:51.541 --> 00:09:53.364
- [Roadhog] Shut up.

00:09:53.364 --> 00:09:54.478
- [Hammeh] Roadhog will
occasionally come out

00:09:54.478 --> 00:09:56.003
with this when he sees
an enemy Junkrat die.

00:09:56.003 --> 00:09:58.325
- [Roadhog] Someone finally shut him up.

00:09:58.325 --> 00:10:00.351
- [Hammeh] And when he
kills an enemy Junkrat,

00:10:00.351 --> 00:10:02.712
he makes it quite clear
what his feelings are.

00:10:02.712 --> 00:10:05.421
- [Roadhog] I'm tired
of hearing your voice.

00:10:05.421 --> 00:10:07.203
- [Hammeh] When Roadhog
watches a Junkrat on his team

00:10:07.203 --> 00:10:09.873
kill something, he's glad
to see Junkrat in action.

00:10:09.873 --> 00:10:12.663
- [Roadhog] About time
you did something useful.

00:10:12.663 --> 00:10:15.777
I'm always saving your skin.

00:10:15.777 --> 00:10:17.545
- [Hammeh] Outside of Junkertown
and the Australian outback,

00:10:17.545 --> 00:10:19.610
Roadhog's actually a
pretty well travelled guy.

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.028
An international crime spree

00:10:21.028 --> 00:10:22.739
clearly gives excellent
travel opportunities.

00:10:22.739 --> 00:10:25.255
He's been all over the
world, from Japan to Paris

00:10:25.255 --> 00:10:26.777
and Mexico to the UK.

00:10:26.777 --> 00:10:28.085
Although being his reserved self,

00:10:28.085 --> 00:10:29.521
when it comes to speaking anyway,

00:10:29.521 --> 00:10:32.085
Roadhog still only has a
little to say on a few maps.

00:10:32.085 --> 00:10:33.120
We've seen and heard

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:34.988
about the Junker's crown
jewel caper in London

00:10:34.988 --> 00:10:36.576
when they took a trip to King's Row.

00:10:36.576 --> 00:10:38.047
It seems as though that
they didn't hang on

00:10:38.047 --> 00:10:39.630
to the spoils of the robbery for long,

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:41.321
if Roadhog's King's Row spawn interaction

00:10:41.321 --> 00:10:42.973
is anything to go by.

00:10:42.973 --> 00:10:44.160
- [Roadhog] Pretty sure they're still mad

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.182
about those jewels we stole.

00:10:47.182 --> 00:10:49.295
I miss that crown.

00:10:49.295 --> 00:10:51.978
- [Hammeh] And when Junkrat
reminisces on the same caper,

00:10:51.978 --> 00:10:54.938
Roadhog even has to remind
Junkrat of his name.

00:10:54.938 --> 00:10:56.708
- [Junkrat] Ah, remember that time

00:10:56.708 --> 00:10:58.684
we stole the crown jewels?

00:10:58.684 --> 00:11:02.322
All hail King Jamison Fawkes the first!

00:11:02.322 --> 00:11:03.739
And Duke Roadhog?

00:11:05.072 --> 00:11:06.883
What is your name, anyways?

00:11:06.883 --> 00:11:08.286
- [Roadhog] Mako.

00:11:08.286 --> 00:11:11.145
- [Hammeh] On picturesque
maps such as Ilios and Nepal,

00:11:11.145 --> 00:11:13.859
we see that Roadhog, or perhaps
Mako in a previous life,

00:11:13.859 --> 00:11:16.676
still has a part of his soul
that appreciates beauty.

00:11:16.676 --> 00:11:18.150
- [Roadhog] Pretty sure they're still mad

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:21.117
about those jewels we stole.

00:11:21.117 --> 00:11:22.617
I miss that crown.

00:11:23.591 --> 00:11:25.244
- [Hammeh] He'll probably
kill someone there anyway,

00:11:25.244 --> 00:11:27.194
of course, but the thought
counts for something, right?

00:11:27.194 --> 00:11:29.551
The Junkers robbed the bank
of Dorado at some point

00:11:29.551 --> 00:11:31.184
as we can see from the
security camera footage

00:11:31.184 --> 00:11:33.400
in the level and Roadhog's
signature canisters

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:34.694
strewn across the vault,

00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:36.250
as well as the map present on the level.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.088
Roadhog has some fond memories of Dorado,

00:11:38.088 --> 00:11:40.391
its vaults, and of course the gold within.

00:11:40.391 --> 00:11:43.641
- [Roadhog] Ooh, they stocked up again.

00:11:44.839 --> 00:11:49.006
Now I know why they call
this place Dorado. (laughing)

00:11:49.998 --> 00:11:51.140
- [Hammeh] Dorado's very name, of course,

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.864
is most likely a nod to El Dorado,

00:11:52.864 --> 00:11:55.999
a 16th or so century
myth of a city or empire

00:11:55.999 --> 00:11:57.601
of golden wealth in South America.

00:11:57.601 --> 00:11:59.615
Roadhog knowing a little
of his South American

00:11:59.615 --> 00:12:02.065
and Spanish conquistador history there.

00:12:02.065 --> 00:12:03.238
Thanks very much for tuning in

00:12:03.238 --> 00:12:04.875
to my hero voiceline and story series.

